{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>Abaddon and Death</b> — they are the dead. The ancients told us: that even they heard from others that man cannot know these matters, and that only the Creator alone knows, who created the four foundations, and they are: earth, heaven, wind, and water. And they are mentioned in the two verses, and He sees new wonders in the words of the rain — therefore it says: בעשותו למטר חק (when He made a decree for the rain)."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {0 "The phrase 'the two verses' is obscure; the reference to unspecified verses about the four elements is left unresolved. The sentence 'והוא יראה פלאים חדשים בדברי המטר' is rendered hyper-literally as it may be a quotation or paraphrase whose source is unclear."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:03:52.974504521Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}